NODE id=matrix/executor/tool.isCacheable kind=func
  digest=b3:1cb4db4d6d3c0b0ac5c81b58243aabcead8f3f3b731ed1fee6c4f22b42d8bbca file=executor/tool/registry.go range=58:69 lang=go exported=false byte_range=1813:2380
  sig=func isCacheable(name, sideEffect string) bool
  doc=isCacheable reports whether a tool's results may be cached, given its\nserver-local name and declared side-effect class. Both conditions must\nhold: the name must be in the explicit allow-list AND the side-effect\nclass must be a read-class (SideEffectRead). The double gate means a\ntool named web_search that someone later retags as "write" stops\nbeing cached automatically — defense in depth against manifest drift.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/executor/tool/registry.go

